0,0,0,0,100,65,128,14,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,64,22,4,232,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,241,255,159,241,64,242,6,48,40,79,0,0,0,0,73,69,78,68,174,66,96,130],"annotations":[{"id":"1775000114469","neuronKeys":["[#f37f5]","[#651c6]","[#0b566]"],"edgeStrings":[],"description":"This Fixed Action Pattern has a sequence of 3 discrete events controlled by these 3 neurons.","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775000143271","neuronKeys":[],"edgeStrings":["[#4f5d2]_#_[#080b1]"],"description":"Activate the sequence by stimulating the distance sensor at a near distance","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775000204762","neuronKeys":["[#080b1]","[#f37f5]"],"edgeStrings":["[#080b1]_#_[#f37f5]","[#f37f5]_#_[#080b1]"],"description":"Once activated, a Reccurent Pair of neurons will activate eachother indefinitely until they get an inhibitory signal.","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775000247219","neuronKeys":[],"edgeStrings":["[#f37f5]_#_[#58d93]","[#f37f5]_#_[#8f0fc]","[#f37f5]_#_[#651c6]","[#f37f5]_#_[#15f48]"],"description":"The first action drives the motors in reverse, glowing red with light, and the signal is passed to the next neuron","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775000317413","neuronKeys":["[#651c6]"],"edgeStrings":[],"description":"For each step in the sequence after the first, we use delay neurons. The delay time determines how long each step will activate for.","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775000367190","neuronKeys":["[#dd5a5]","[#651c6]"],"edgeStrings":["[#651c6]_#_[#dd5a5]","[#dd5a5]_#_[#080b1]","[#dd5a5]_#_[#f37f5]"],"description":"When the delay neuron begins to fire, it will pass the signal to an inhibitory neuron which will stop the first action from firing!","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775000457090","neuronKeys":[],"edgeStrings":["[#651c6]_#_[#15f48]","[#651c6]_#_[#235da]","[#651c6]_#_[#0b566]"],"description":"The second action will do a turn forward and to the right, while spikerbot lights up yellow. It passes the signal to the next neuron in the sequence.","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775000601757","neuronKeys":[],"edgeStrings":["[#0b566]_#_[#22937]","[#0b566]_#_[#15f48]"],"description":"The final action turns the robot left, and glows green.","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775000567754","neuronKeys":["[#dd5a5]"],"edgeStrings":["[#0b566]_#_[#dd5a5]","[#dd5a5]_#_[#080b1]","[#651c6]_#_[#dd5a5]","[#dd5a5]_#_[#f37f5]"],"description":"Every step besides the first step will trigger the inhibitory neuron. This prevents the sequence from being interrupted by new stimuli from the distance sensor.","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775000673105","neuronKeys":["[#651c6]","[#0b566]","[#dd5a5]"],"edgeStrings":[],"description":"When the delay neurons stop firing, the inhibitory neuron will stop supressing the input neurons, enabling us to retrigger the input!","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775000755318","neuronKeys":["[#080b1]"],"edgeStrings":[],"description":"Experiment with how you stimulate the input neuron. You can use sensory input, trigger it with other neurons, or even change its behavior to activate with remote control!","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775490767232","neuronKeys":[],"edgeStrings":["[#c54ee]_#_[#db1a5]","[#c54ee]_#_[#dcf52]"],"description":"What will happen when you reduce or remove the inhibitory connections? Many neurological disorders are considered to be caused by inhibitory disfunction.","thumbnail":""}],"info":{"title":"Fixed Action Pattern","description":"Preforms a discrete motion pattern requiring inhibition.","author":"User","version":"1.0.1","timestamp":"2026-04-08T15:31:01.926665"}}